VanaParse 1.1.0.0 - Update Notes

This update focuses on simplifying VanaParse, improving HUD clarity and making commands more intuitive.

***HIGHLIGHTS***
Simplified command structure using a natural verb-first format such as:

//vp show magic
//vp hide magic
//vp filter Aminon
//vp unfilter Aminon
//vp report full party

Expanded reporting so users can choose:
- what to report
- who to report
- where to send it

Added detailed player performance reporting with support for:
- Physical
- Magic
- Ranged
- Healing
- Recovery/Status Removal
- Pet contributions
- Defense and damage taken

Added deeper Magic tracking by spell, element, cast count, average damage and Magic Burst performance.
Added Recovery/Status tracking for actions like Healing Waltz, Erase, Poisona and similar effects.
Improved Dynamic HUD behavior and category visibility.
Added dedicated Magic damage support while allowing entire categories to be shown or hidden.
Improved target tracking and target-specific damage handling.
Improved HUD alignment with numeric columns right-justified and text columns left-justified.
Removed redundant, outdated and low-value report paths.
Cleaned the release package to remove historical, validation, character-specific and unnecessary development files.

Continued support for filters, named splits, compact views, detailed reports and paced chat output.

The goal of this revision is to make VanaParse easier to understand and use without sacrificing the deeper combat analysis available when needed.
